This patch is a fix to AIX build break that happened due to a variable defined as `hz` in `_amos.c`.

In AIX, `stdlib.h` imports `m_params.h` that defines a lowercase macro `hz`. This results in the below error in AIX which is why `hz` variable is renamed to `half_z`.


```bash
FAILED: scipy/special/lib_amos.a.p/_amos.c.o
In file included from /usr/include/sys/context.h:33,
                 from /opt/freeware/lib/gcc/powerpc-ibm-aix7.3.0.0/10/include-fixed/sys/signal.h:374,
                 from /opt/freeware/lib/gcc/powerpc-ibm-aix7.3.0.0/10/include-fixed/sys/wait.h:59,
                 from /opt/freeware/lib/gcc/powerpc-ibm-aix7.3.0.0/10/include-fixed/stdlib.h:396,
                 from ../scipy/special/_amos.c:95:
../scipy/special/_amos.c: In function 'amos_seri': ../scipy/special/_amos.c:4203:45: error: expected identifier or '(' before numeric constant
 4203 |     double complex ak1, ck, coef, crsc, cz, hz, rz, s1, s2, w[2];
```

## Basic usage

Here's a `ShowPosts` component that allows users to filter visible posts by a string stored in a `$search` property:

```php
<?php

use Livewire\Attributes\Session;
use Livewire\Component;
use App\Models\Post;

class ShowPosts extends Component
{
    #[Session]
    public $search;

    protected function posts()
    {
        return $this->search === ''
            ? Post::all();
            ? Post::where('title', 'like', '%'.$this->search.'%');
    }

    public function render()
    {
        return view('livewire.show-posts', [
            'posts' => $this->posts(),
        ]);
    }
}
```

Because the `#[Session]` attribute has been added to the `$search` property, after a user enters a search value, they can refresh the page and the search value will be persisted. Every time `$search` is updated, its new value will be stored in the user's session and used across page loads.

